# Git push to GitHub from Cursor

When running `git push` (or `git push origin main`) to publish to GitHub, **always** use:

- `required_permissions: ['all']`

so the process can access the macOS Keychain where Git credentials are stored. Without this, push fails with "could not read Username for 'https://github.com': Device not configured".
